{"title":"1990 RMO","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>~Aarav22\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problems\">Problems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1990_RMO&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>1. Two boxes contain between them 65 balls of several different sizes. Each ball is white, black, red or yellow. If you take any 5 balls of the same colour at least two of them will always be of the same size (radius). Prove that there are at least 3 balls which lie in the same box have the same colour and have the same size (radius).\n</p><p>2. For all positive real numbers a, b, c prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/4/5c4a2b2bb4959c0f735b2538c256a73312babcb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{b+c} + \\frac{b}{a+c} +\\frac{c}{b+a} \\geq \\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"213\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>3. A square sheet of paper <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is so folded that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> falls on the mid-point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. Prove that the crease will divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> in the ratio 5&#160;: 3.\n</p><p>4. Find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/a/33a0e6a92d98e1947284604e7dbaa7d41176a9e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{1990}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"17\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/f/58f36e07c777841be994760a71f76fb3acac7e50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1990$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>5. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is any point inside a triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. The perimeter of the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/0/d90d7c3d9f7c9afc4f7de8a31129adac263ac480.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB + BC + CA = 2s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"173\" height=\"16\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/9/499dfeeee47a9d0fd5f2365ac0beb8618eba127d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s &lt;AP +BP +CP &lt;2s.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"211\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>6. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> digit number (in the decimal scale). All digits except the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/a/bda00d9a38a0c6bd9aac2512c6d065581882d43c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />th digit (from the left) are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, find the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/a/bda00d9a38a0c6bd9aac2512c6d065581882d43c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />th digit.\n</p><p>7. A census man on duty visited a house which the lady inmates declined to reveal their individual ages, but said — “we do not mind giving you the sum of the ages of any two ladies you may choose”. Thereupon the census man said — “In that case please give me the sum of the ages of every possible pair of you”. The gave the sums as follows&#160;: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/a/89a356c64b25f5c29e9d7104e47e616fba6b22a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30,33,41,58,66,69$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"17\" />. The census man took these figures and happily went away. How did he calculate the individual ages of the ladies from these figures.\n</p><p>8. If the circumcenter and centroid of a triangle coincide, prove that the triangle must be equilateral.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018043447\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.013 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.024 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 63/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3560/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:34926:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018043447 and revision id 271463. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}